ose status and headers are kept; the\nticket read from `X-Session-Ticket` (32 lowercase hex, on a 200 reply);\nthe protocol version read from `X-MCP-Protocol` (a YYYY-MM-DD date). A\nThen step that finds no kept reply fails rather than passes.\n\nOnly the role in the When step varies, so only it gets a capture group —\nthe other three phrases carry no placeholder, and their patterns are\nanchored literals of the *catalogue phrase*, not of a scenario line.\n\n## Required Changes\n\n### Change #1: the suite's shared state and its observation helpers\n\n**File:** `tests/mcp/steps/state.go`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file).\n**Content:**\n```go\n// Package steps binds the registry steps of the `mcp` suite to code.\n//\n// The suite's state is the MCP server address the Given step resolved\n// and the reply to the session's opening the When step kept; every Then\n// step reads that reply.\npackage steps\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\t// portEnv and defaultPort are the architecture's address mapping:\n\t// 127.0.0.1 at MCP_PORT, 7411 when it is unset.\n\tportEnv     = \"MCP_PORT\"\n\tdefaultPort = \"7411\"\n\tlocalHost   = \"127.0.0.1\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\thealthTimeout       = 5 * time.Second\n\thealthPollInterval  = 50 * time.Millisecond\n\thealthReqTimeout    = time.Second\n\topenSessionTimeout  = 10 * time.Second\n\tinitializeRequest   = `{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\"}`\n)\n\n// Reply is what a Then step may read of the session's opening: the\n// status code and the headers of the server's reply to initialize.\ntype Reply struct {\n\tStatus int\n\tHeader http.Header\n}\n\n// State is the state the suite's step definitions share.\ntype State struct {\n\taddr  string\n\treply *Reply\n}\n\n// New returns the state one scenario's steps run against.\nfunc New() *State {\n\treturn &State{}\n}\n\n// Addr is the MCP server address the Given step resolved