e session was not granted a ticket: expected status 200 with a %s header of 32 lowercase hexadecimal characters, got status %d with %s: %q\",\n\t\t\tticketHeader, reply.Status, ticketHeader, ticket,\n\t\t)\n\t}\n\n\tif !regexp.MustCompile(ticketPattern).MatchString(ticket) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\n\t\t\t\"the session was not granted a ticket: expected the %s header of the 200 reply to be 32 lowercase hexadecimal characters, got %q\",\n\t\t\tticketHeader, ticket,\n\t\t)\n\t}\n\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// serverNamesProtocolVersion asserts the reply to initialize names the\n// protocol version as a YYYY-MM-DD date.\nfunc serverNamesProtocolVersion(state *State, _ []string) error {\n\treply, err := state.openedSession()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\tversion := reply.Header.Get(protocolHeader)\n\tif _, perr := time.Parse(protocolLayout, version); perr != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\n\t\t\t\"the server did not name its protocol version: expected the %s header of the session's opening to be a date in YYYY-MM-DD form, got %q (reply status %d)\",\n\t\t\tprotocolHeader, version, reply.Status,\n\t\t)\n\t}\n\n\treturn nil\n}\n```\n\n## Constraints on applying this\n\n- Create both files with **Write**; they are new. If `tests/mcp/steps/`\n  already holds Go files from an earlier pass, do **not** overwrite them:\n  Read them, add only the missing `suite.Step(...)` lines to the existing\n  `Register` function with **Edit**, and reuse the state type already\n  there instead of introducing `State` a second time.\n- Every one of the four definitions is registered in the single\n  `Register` function — do not add a second registration function.\n- Do not relax any pattern, do not add a definition for a step opening\n  with `llm:` or `judge:` (this suite has none), and do not modify\n  `docs/scenarios.yaml` or any file outside `tests/mcp/steps/`.\n- Do not create `tests/mcp/scenarios/` or edit the generated\n  `tests/mcp/mcp_test.go`; they are outside this fix's write r